TASK B109
	TITLE "A brigade run that receives SIGTERM or SIGINT, or that brigade runs stop names, stops"
		+ "the client's process group with the grace and the kill of the wall limit and ends on the"
		+ "outcome stopped, so that no client outlives its run"
	STATUS implemented
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.F0
	COMPONENT "runs"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "brigade run that receives SIGTERM or SIGINT while a segment runs sends SIGTERM to the"
		+ "process group of the client, waits the grace the wall limit waits, 30 s, sends SIGKILL"
		+ "to the group when the client still lives, and waits for the process: when brigade run"
		+ "exits, no process of the client's group lives"
		IMPL "brigade/system/stop_process_group.py::def stop_process_group(process:"
			+ "subprocess.Popen, grace_before_kill_s: float) -> None:"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/run_segment.py::stop_process_group(process, limit.grace_before_kill_s)"
		IMPL "brigade/commands/run.py::with StopSignalReceiver() as stop:"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segment.py::def"
			+ "test_should_stop_the_group_of_the_client_and_end_the_segment_stopped(self):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/system/test_stop_process_group.py::def"
			+ "test_should_kill_the_group_once_the_grace_is_over(self):"
	SPEC "the segment ends with the outcome stopped: run.finished is appended with outcome stopped,"
		+ "its exit null and its nulls naming the stop, as those of a segment cut at the wall limit"
		+ "name the cut; no further segment is launched, whatever the progress file holds;"
		+ "result.json is written with outcome stopped, after the ledger events, and brigade run"
		+ "exits 21, the code DESC 4 of the decision on exit codes gives stopped"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/run_segment.py::ending = _describe_ending(STOPPED_OUTCOME,"
			+ "STOPPED_BY_A_SIGNAL, launch.session_id, measured_ms)"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/describe_finished.py::ENDING_REASONS = {WALL_LIMIT_OUTCOME:"
			+ "WALL_LIMIT_CUT, STOPPED_OUTCOME: STOPPED_BY_A_SIGNAL}"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/decide_run_exit_code.py::\"stopped\": 21,"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_describe_finished.py::def"
			+ "test_should_name_the_stop_and_the_reason_a_stopped_segment_is_left_unmeasured(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_run.py::def"
			+ "test_should_stop_the_client_of_a_foreground_run_sent_sigint_and_exit_21(self):"
	SPEC "a signal received before the client is spawned or between two segments ends the run the"
		+ "same way, on outcome stopped and exit 21, no further segment launched"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/run_segment.py::return _record_stop_before_launch(number,"
			+ "launch.session_id)"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segment.py::def"
			+ "test_should_end_the_segment_stopped_without_spawning_the_client(self):"
	SPEC "the record of the stopped client in runs/<id>/processes.jsonl has the outcome stopped and"
		+ "its exit null, apart from cut, the wall limit"
		IMPL "brigade/system/process_trace.py::STOPPED = \"stopped\""
		IMPL "brigade/runs/run_segment.py::return None, STOPPED"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segment.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_the_client_stopped_in_the_trail(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_run.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_the_stop_in_the_finished_event_and_in_the_processes_of_the_run(self):"
	SPEC "brigade runs stop <run> sends SIGTERM to the pid of runs/<id>/pid and exits 0 once the"
		+ "run has finished on stopped; a run already finished, or holding no pid file, is refused"
		+ "with exit 1 and a message naming the run and why"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/stop_run.py::def stop_run(state_root: Path, run_id: str) -> dict:"
		IMPL "brigade/commands/runs_stop.py::path=(\"runs\", \"stop\"),"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_stop_a_detached_run_and_exit_0_once_it_finished_stopped(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_refuse_a_finished_run_naming_its_outcome(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def test_should_refuse_a_run_holding_no_pid_file(self):"
	SPEC "a detached run is stopped the same way by a SIGTERM or SIGINT sent to the pid of"
		+ "runs/<id>/pid, the process brigade run --detach re-executes; brigade runs list then"
		+ "shows it finished with outcome stopped, never dead"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_run.py::def"
			+ "test_should_stop_the_client_of_a_detached_run_sent_sigterm_and_list_the_run_finished_stopped(self):"
	SPEC "tests/cli prove it through the fake client with a delay: a detached run sent SIGTERM"
		+ "through the pid of runs/<id>/pid ends with the client's process gone, result.json"
		+ "carrying outcome stopped, one run.finished event with outcome stopped and brigade runs"
		+ "list showing the run finished; a foreground run sent SIGINT ends the same way; brigade"
		+ "runs stop ends a detached run the same way and exits 1 on a finished run; a client that"
		+ "ignores SIGTERM is killed after the grace, in a unit row with a short grace as"
		+ "tests/unit/system/test_wait_within_limit.py proves the wall limit"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_run.py::class BrigadeRunStoppedBySignalTest(RunTestCase):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::class BrigadeRunsStopOfARunningRunTest(RunsTestCase):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/system/test_wait_within_limit.py::def"
			+ "test_should_kill_the_group_once_the_grace_is_over_when_the_run_is_stopped(self):"
