TASK B113
	TITLE "brigade runs show <id> --follow prints the journal of a run as it is written, until the"
		+ "run ends"
	STATUS implemented
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.F0
	COMPONENT "runs"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "brigade runs show <id> --follow prints the summary and the journal as --log does, then"
		+ "each record appended to runs/<id>/journal.jsonl, read every journal_poll_s seconds of"
		+ "config.toml, until the state of the run is finished or dead; the journal is read once"
		+ "more after that state is seen, so that no record written before result.json is missed"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/run_follower.py::def read_records(self) -> list[dict]:"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_follower.py::def"
			+ "test_should_read_the_last_record_of_a_run_that_ends_while_it_reads_the_run(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_read_the_run_again_only_every_journal_poll_s_seconds(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_print_a_record_written_after_it_started_and_exit_0_once_the_run_is_done(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_print_the_journal_as_log_does_then_the_state_and_outcome_of_the_run(self):"
	SPEC "once the run has ended, --follow prints its state and its outcome and exits as brigade"
		+ "run does: 0 when the outcome is done, 1 when it is failed or wall_limit or the run is"
		+ "dead"
		IMPL "brigade/commands/runs_show.py::def _decide_exit_code(document: dict) -> int:"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_exit_as_brigade_run_does_by_the_outcome_of_the_run(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def test_should_exit_1_once_it_sees_the_run_dead(self):"
	SPEC "a line of the journal not yet whole is printed once whole"
		IMPL "brigade/runs/journal_reader.py::def read_whole_records(self) -> list[dict]:"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_journal_reader.py::def"
			+ "test_should_read_a_line_once_it_is_whole(self):"
	SPEC "SIGINT or SIGTERM ends the follow alone, with exit code 0 and no traceback: the run"
		+ "followed, detached in a session of its own, runs on"
		IMPL "brigade/system/poll_until_signalled.py::def poll_until_signalled(poll: Callable[[],"
			+ "bool], interval_s: float) -> bool:"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def"
			+ "test_should_exit_0_on_a_signal_and_leave_the_run_running(self):"
	SPEC "--follow given with --json is a usage error: exit code 2, one line on stderr, stdout"
		+ "empty"
		IMPL "brigade/commands/runs_show.py::def _read_request(options):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::def test_should_refuse_json_as_a_usage_error(self):"
	SPEC "tests/cli prove, on a detached run of the fake client, that --follow prints a record"
		+ "written after the command started and exits with the code of the run once it has ended,"
		+ "and that a SIGINT sent to the follow exits 0 while the run is still running"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_runs.py::class"
			+ "BrigadeRunsShowFollowOfARunningRunTest(RunsFollowTestCase):"
	DELIVERED_BY 85
	RATIONALE "@TASK.B79 writes the journal live, but runs show reads it once and exits: watch of"
		+ "runs show --log keeps the start of a journal longer than the terminal and cuts its end,"
		+ "the user's finding of 2026-10-09, and tail -f of journal.jsonl prints raw JSON records"
		REF @TASK.B79
	RATIONALE "in @MILESTONE.F0 and first among its drafts, at the user's request: following a run"
		+ "is how a wave of brigade on itself is watched"
		REF @MILESTONE.F0
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-09 in the refinement of B113 that the journal of a run"
		+ "must scroll as it is written: the REJECTED of a --follow of brigade in"
