TASK B114
	TITLE "A segment reaching its wall-time limit is stopped between two steps where its client"
		+ "supports it, its result kept, and cut by signal only as the backstop"
	STATUS todo
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.F0
	COMPONENT "adapters"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "config.toml takes soft_limit_margin_s, a positive number of seconds, 120 by default; the"
		+ "soft limit of a segment is its wall-time limit minus that margin, and a wall-time limit"
		+ "not above the margin gives no soft limit"
	SPEC "the launch-argv and resume-argv requests carry stop_at, the instant of the soft limit in"
		+ "UTC, ISO 8601 to the second with the suffix Z, computed when the segment is launched,"
		+ "null when the segment has no soft limit; an adapter whose probe does not declare"
		+ "graceful_stop ignores it"
	SPEC "the probe answer may declare the feature graceful_stop; its fallback, the hard cut at the"
		+ "wall-time limit, is listed in DESC 2 of the decision naming no AI client outside its"
		+ "adapters, in the fallbacks of brigade adapter matrix and in a column Graceful stop of"
		+ "the two tables of the README that brigade adapter matrix generates and of the"
		+ "hand-written table of brigade-client-vibe"
	SPEC "the parse-result answer may carry the outcome soft_limit, a session the client ended"
		+ "itself once stop_at had passed; brigade records such a segment in run.finished and"
		+ "segments/<n>/result.json as it records a segment ended done, its session, steps, usage"
		+ "and cost_usd included"
	SPEC "a segment ending on soft_limit continues the run as a segment cut at the wall-time limit"
		+ "does: a signal.recorded wall_limit_reached carrying wall_limit_s, then a fresh segment"
		+ "from the progress file while hand-overs remain and the file is not empty"
	SPEC "the hard cut is unchanged: a client still running at the wall-time limit gets SIGTERM to"
		+ "its process group and SIGKILL 30 s later, and the segment ends on wall_limit, whether"
		+ "stop_at was passed or not"
	SPEC "soft_limit has the exit code 13 that DESC 3 gives it in the decision on exit codes;"
		+ "brigade run and brigade runs show --follow exit 13 for a run whose last segment ended on"
		+ "it"
	SPEC "the Claude Code adapter declares graceful_stop; given a stop_at, its argv adds --settings"
		+ "with one PostToolUse hook of matcher *, whose command, carried whole in that value with"
		+ "no file and no path of the machine, exits 0 and prints {\"continue\": false,"
		+ "\"stopReason\": <the soft limit>} once stop_at has passed and nothing before, for the"
		+ "main session and its sub-agents alike; given no stop_at, the argv carries no --settings"
	SPEC "the Claude Code adapter answers outcome soft_limit for a result event of subtype success"
		+ "whose terminal_reason is hook_stopped, whatever its final message, and reads its"
		+ "session, steps, usage and cost_usd as for a session ended done"
	SPEC "the fake adapter, graceful_stop in its features setting and given a stop_at, prints its"
		+ "recording once stop_at has passed, so that a recording ending on outcome soft_limit"
		+ "plays a cooperative stop"
	SPEC "unit rows of tests/unit/adapters/clients/test_claude_code.py pin the --settings value"
		+ "given a stop_at and its absence without one, the hook command run before and after its"
		+ "stop_at printing nothing then the stop, and the outcome soft_limit read from a result"
		+ "event with terminal_reason hook_stopped, done from the same event without it"
	SPEC "tests/cli prove through the fake client declaring graceful_stop that a run whose first"
		+ "segment ends on soft_limit before its wall-time limit records it in run.finished with"
		+ "its cost_usd, launches a second segment from the progress file and exits 0 once that one"
		+ "is done; and through the fake client declaring nothing, with a delay past the wall-time"
		+ "limit, that the segment is cut on wall_limit as before"
	AFTER @TASK.B84
	AFTER @TASK.B85
	AFTER @TASK.B102
	RATIONALE "today a segment reaching its wall-time limit is killed mid-step:"
		+ "brigade/system/wait_within_limit.py:23-29 sends SIGTERM to the client's process group,"
		+ "then SIGKILL after GRACE_BEFORE_KILL_S, 30 s, brigade/runs/run_segment.py:41; the user"
		+ "asked on 2026-10-09 for a cut that lets the agent finish the step in progress"
		REF @DECISION.EveryRunIsHeldOnTheClockAtThirtySecondsPerStepOfItsCap
	RATIONALE "a cooperative stop keeps the client's result object, hence cost_usd, which a cut"
		+ "segment lacks even once @TASK.B84 has merged: no price table is held, so a cut segment"
		+ "has no cost_usd; B84 also gives the segment its session from launch, which this task"
		+ "builds on"
		REF @TASK.B84
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-09 against a Claude Code hook in the core: brigade stays"
		+ "as agnostic as it can and the client-specific part sits in one module; the core computes"
		+ "the soft limit and records the outcome, the contract carries an optional feature with"
		+ "its fallback, brigade/adapters/clients/claude_code.py alone knows --settings,"
		+ "PostToolUse and terminal_reason, and brigade-client-vibe, declaring nothing, keeps the"
		+ "hard cut"
		REF @DECISION.BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	RATIONALE "@DECISION.AKeyAddedToTheClientContractIsRequiredOfEveryAdapter binds keys added to"
		+ "an answer, and no answer gains one: graceful_stop is a value of the existing features"
		+ "key of the probe, as step_count is, soft_limit a value of the existing outcome key of"
		+ "parse-result, and stop_at a key of a request; brigade-client-vibe reads the keys of its"
		+ "requests by name, read on 2026-10-09, so stop_at changes nothing for it"
		REF @DECISION.AKeyAddedToTheClientContractIsRequiredOfEveryAdapter
	RATIONALE "verified on 2026-10-09 by an exploration run on Claude Code 2.1.295, model haiku:"
		+ "--settings with a PostToolUse hook printing {\"continue\": false} once a deadline has"
		+ "passed stops the session right after the current tool call, the next step never issued;"
		+ "the process exits 0 with a result event of subtype success, is_error false,"
		+ "total_cost_usd, usage and num_turns, terminal_reason hook_stopped being the only field"
		+ "telling the stop from a normal end; SIGTERM mid-tool exits 143 in under 1 s with no"
		+ "result event"
	RATIONALE "the margin covers the longest foreground step: in the same runs a Bash sleep 20"
		+ "passing the deadline was not interrupted, the stop coming 15 s after the deadline, once"
		+ "the call had ended; Claude Code moved a Bash sleep 25 and sleep 60 to the background at"
		+ "once, a threshold inferred from these runs only"
	RATIONALE "PostToolUse fires for a sub-agent's tool calls, its input carrying agent_id and the"
		+ "same session_id; continue false returned for every call stopped the sub-agent, then the"
		+ "main session at the PostToolUse of its Agent call, terminal_reason hook_stopped, the"
		+ "sub-agent's transcript complete; claude -p inherits the hooks and the agent of the"
		+ "user's ~/.claude/settings.json and --settings merges with them, so the hook coexists"
		+ "with them and agent_type of its input is not relied on"
	RATIONALE "not tested on 2026-10-09: parallel tool calls in one turn, Stop hooks, a sub-agent"
		+ "running in the background"
	RATIONALE "soft_limit, not stopped, which @TASK.B109 gives a run stopped by a signal; 13, the"
		+ "next warning of @DECISION.EveryEndOfARunHasItsOwnExitCodeRangedBySeverity after"
		+ "wall_limit 11 and turn_limit 12, that decision giving every end of a run a code of its"
		+ "own"
		REF @TASK.B109
		REF @DECISION.EveryEndOfARunHasItsOwnExitCodeRangedBySeverity
	RATIONALE "a segment ending on soft_limit appends the signal of @TASK.B85, wall_limit_reached:"
		+ "the cause is the clock, and the outcome soft_limit already tells how the segment"
		+ "stopped; the user's ruling of 2026-10-10 in the refinement of B85"
		REF @TASK.B85
	SOURCE "the user's words of 2026-10-09: \"il y a pas moyen de faire en sorte que l'on coupe un"
		+ "agent en le laissant terminer une step en cours?\"; after the session proposed a Claude"
		+ "Code hook, \"ok mais ça veut dire qu'on fait du spécifique. J'aimerais que l'on soit au"
		+ "maximum agnostique, et qu'on isole le spécifique dans un module dédié.\"; then \"oui\""
		+ "to the split into core, client contract, Claude Code adapter, fake adapter and"
		+ "brigade-client-vibe, and to the verification of the facts"

TASK B115
